{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21f77e39d99b57bc5b74", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Chemical Kinetics - Test 5", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 30, "totalQuestions": 20, "totalMarks": 80, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d91", "totalMarks": 80, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 20, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9257"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9254", "title": "Chemistry Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d91", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f91ed", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b85"], "concepts": ["60e56768499d1e49588f8ee2"], "question": {"text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>NO</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8652;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>NOCl</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo></math><br />This reaction was studied at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> and the following data was obtained</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mi>run</mi></mtd><mtd><mo>[</mo><mi>NO</mi><msub><mo>]</mo><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\" separators=\"|\"><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>&#8197;&#8197;&#8197;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0.10</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0.10</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0.18</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0.10</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0.20</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0.35</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0.20</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0.20</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1.40</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mi>NO</mi><msub><mo>]</mo><mn>0</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>0</mn></msub></math> are the initial concentrations and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math> is the initial reaction rate. The overall order of the reaction is<br />(Round off to the Nearest Integer).</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "71b022", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f91ee"}, {"id": "cfc9c0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f91ef"}, {"id": "22dd7c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f91f0"}, {"id": "ae6110", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f91f1"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f91f2", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52f6"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5660"], "question": {"text": "Time required for completion of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>99</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of first order reaction is ________ times of half life <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></math> of the reaction"}, "options": [{"id": "ebc59b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f91f3"}, {"id": "6b882c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f91f4"}, {"id": "eb052f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f91f5"}, {"id": "28c7e7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f91f6"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f91f7", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4793"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f2c"], "question": {"text": "<p>The number of correct statement/s from the following is _____ .</p><p>A.Larger the activation energy, smaller is the value of the rate constant.</p><p>B. The higher is the activation energy, higher is the value of the temperature coefficient.</p><p>C. At lower temperatures, increase in temperature causes more change in the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></math> than at higher temperature.</p><p>D. A plot of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ln</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></math> vs <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> is a straight line with slope equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>Ea</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mfrac></math></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "8b61a7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f91f8"}, {"id": "a292ab", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f91f9"}, {"id": "bc3b08", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f91fa"}, {"id": "ad947a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f91fb"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f91fc", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b85"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b56"], "question": {"text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>NO</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p><p>The above reaction has been studied at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>800</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. The related data are given in the table below</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>Reaction&nbsp;serial number</td>\t\t\t<td>Initial pressure of<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>kPa</mi></math>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>Initial Pressure<br />\t\t\tof&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NO</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>kPa</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td>Initial rate&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>dp</mi></mrow><mi>dt</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mo>/</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>kPa</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>65</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>135</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>65</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>033</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>38</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>65</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>214</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>19</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>65</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>106</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table><p>The order of the reaction with respect to NO is____</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "ea3c0a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f91fd"}, {"id": "628706", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f91fe"}, {"id": "b13e8f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f91ff"}, {"id": "dcf0f9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9200"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9201", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52f6"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e67"], "question": {"text": "Consider the two different first order reactions given below\n\\(\\mathrm{A}+\\mathrm{B} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{C}\\) (Reaction 1\\()\\)\n\\(P \\rightarrow Q\\) (Reaction 2)\nThe ratio of the half life of Reaction 1 : Reaction 2 is \\(5: 2\\). If \\(t_1\\) and \\(t_2\\) represent the time taken to complete \\(2 / 3^{\\text {rd }}\\) and \\(45^{\\text {th }}\\) of Reaction 1 and Reaction 2, respectively, then the value of the ratio \\(t_1: t_2\\) is ______ \\(\\times 10^{-1}\\) (nearest integer).\n[Given : \\(\\log _{10}(3)=0.477\\) and \\(\\log _{10}(5)=0.699\\)]"}, "options": [{"id": "b52d75", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9202"}, {"id": "d1e83d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9203"}, {"id": "b70fcd", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9204"}, {"id": "5aec03", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9205"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9206", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4793"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b474c"], "question": {"text": "<p>The decomposition of formic acid on gold surface follows first order kinetics. If the rate constant at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and the activation energy <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>488</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, the rate constant at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> is&nbsp;_________&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. (Round of to the Nearest Integer).</p><p>(Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>314</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "13aa99", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9207"}, {"id": "d61b2c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9208"}, {"id": "8486c2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9209"}, {"id": "9d5e48", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f920a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f920b", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b85"], "concepts": ["61489977457fcc27bc16f024"], "question": {"text": "For a given chemical reaction&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#947;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#947;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#947;</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#947;</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math>. Concentration of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>&nbsp;changes from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mmol</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>dm</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mmol</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>dm</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;Rate of&nbsp;appearance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;times the rate of disappearance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> which is twice the rate of disappearance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>. The rate of appearance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math>&nbsp;has been experimentally determined to be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mmol</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>dm</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;Therefore the rate of&nbsp;reaction is____<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>mmol</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>dm</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;(Nearest Integer)"}, "options": [{"id": "0f1ba4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f920c"}, {"id": "6d4e0a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f920d"}, {"id": "4e3a13", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f920e"}, {"id": "bef6ec", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f920f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9210", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52f6"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5660"], "question": {"text": "If <math><mrow><mn>75</mn><mi>%</mi></mrow></math> of a first order reaction was completed in <math><mrow><mn>90</mn></mrow></math> minutes, <math><mrow><mn>60</mn><mi>%</mi></mrow></math> of the same reaction would be completed in approximately (in minutes) _____<br />(Take: <math><mrow><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0.30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>;</mo><mi>log</mi><mn>2.5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0.40</mn></mrow></math>)"}, "options": [{"id": "381236", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9211"}, {"id": "d0cc5e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9212"}, {"id": "0f2cfb", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9213"}, {"id": "bc6a17", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9214"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9215", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4793"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f2c"], "question": {"text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math></p><p>The rate constants of the above reaction at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>03</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>05</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> respectively. The activation energy for the reaction is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math> (Nearest integer)</p><p>(Given : In <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>log</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>70</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>log</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>48</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>30</mn></math></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "34a1ee", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9216"}, {"id": "8d03a6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9217"}, {"id": "f311a3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9218"}, {"id": "4109d1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9219"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f921a", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b85"], "concepts": ["60e56768499d1e49588f8ee2"], "question": {"text": "Consider the following data for the given reaction<br/><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>HI</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>→</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mi>HI</mi><mfenced><msup><mi>molL</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mfenced></mtd><mtd><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>005</mn></mtd><mtd><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>01</mn><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>02</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>Rate <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>molL</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mn>7</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>The order of the reaction is __________."}, "options": [{"id": "a92857", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f921b"}, {"id": "6d76f9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f921c"}, {"id": "65d81e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f921d"}, {"id": "0345f8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f921e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f921f", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52f6"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e67"], "question": {"text": "<p>A first order reaction has the rate constant, &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The number of correct statement/s from the following is/are Given: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>log</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>48</mn></math>.</p><p>A. Reaction completes in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>.<br />B. The reaction has a half-life of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>.<br />C. The time required for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></math> completion is 25 times the time required for 90%&nbsp;completion.<br />D. The degree of dissociation is equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>kt</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>.<br />E. The rate and the rate constant have the same unit.</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "538d76", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9220"}, {"id": "665c72", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9221"}, {"id": "71e528", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9222"}, {"id": "5ce495", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9223"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9224", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4793"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f2c"], "question": {"text": "<p>The rate constants for decomposition of acetaldehyde have been measured over the temperature range <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>700</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>. The data has been analysed by plotting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>lnk</mi></math> vs <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> graph. The value of activation energy for the reaction is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>kJmol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. (Nearest integer) (Given : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>31</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fb3702c39-574c-49b4-87de-97cc476aac52-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 214px; height: 200px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "9572ff", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9225"}, {"id": "301b57", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9226"}, {"id": "e51aca", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9227"}, {"id": "7396ff", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9228"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9229", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b85"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b56"], "question": {"text": "Given below are two statements :\nStatement I: The rate law for the reaction \\(A+B \\rightarrow C\\) is rate \\((r)=k[A]^2[B]\\). When the concentration of both A and B is doubled, the reaction rate is increased \" \\(x\\) \" times.\nStatement II :\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FoaVeD3j4IFh9uP62aNITFptfvri1he25gV4PXXuoEDY.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br />The figure is showing \"the variation in concentration against time plot\" for a \" \\(y\\) \" order reaction.\nThe Value of \\(x+y\\) is ______"}, "options": [{"id": "16d79c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f922a"}, {"id": "3bf049", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f922b"}, {"id": "85249c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f922c"}, {"id": "a529b7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f922d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f922e", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52f6"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5660"], "question": {"text": "For the thermal decomposition of $\\mathrm{N}_2 \\mathrm{O}_5(\\mathrm{~g})$ at constant volume, the following table can be formed, for the reaction mentioned below.\n$2 \\mathrm{~N}_2 \\mathrm{O}_5(\\mathrm{~g}) \\rightarrow 2 \\mathrm{~N}_2 \\mathrm{O}_4(\\mathrm{~g})+\\mathrm{O}_2(\\mathrm{~g})$\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FM8m7iFzbS47yEC1dB1lyISVW_WRSjZOeZs7D15VD2Yk.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>\n$\\mathrm{x}=\\ldots \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{~atm} \\text { [nearest integer] }$\nGiven : Rate constant for the reaction is $4.606 \\times 10^{-2} \\mathrm{~s}^{-1}$."}, "options": [{"id": "96e99d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f922f"}, {"id": "58ed9a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9230"}, {"id": "ecbf42", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9231"}, {"id": "818dd3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9232"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9233", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4793"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f2c"], "question": {"text": "If the activation energy of a reaction is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>80</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, the fraction of molecules at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>700</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>, having enough energy to react to form products is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></msup></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> is (Rounded off to the nearest integer) [Use <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>31</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>]"}, "options": [{"id": "952512", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9234"}, {"id": "23d0c5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9235"}, {"id": "257206", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9236"}, {"id": "b4cc08", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9237"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9238", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52f6"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e67"], "question": {"text": "The rate of first order reaction is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>04</mn><mo> </mo><mi>mol</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math> minutes and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>03</mn><mo> </mo><mi>mol</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn></math> minutes after initiation. Half life of the reaction is ______ minutes. (Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3010</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>log</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4771</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Round off your answer to the nearest integer."}, "options": [{"id": "06b73c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9239"}, {"id": "bdfd2e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f923a"}, {"id": "945b7f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f923b"}, {"id": "3b145f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f923c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f923d", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4793"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f2c"], "question": {"text": "<p>The number of given statement/s which is/are correct is_____</p><p>(A) The stronger the temperature dependence of the rate constant, the higher is the activation energy.</p><p>(B) If a reaction has zero activation energy, its rate is independent of temperature.</p><p>(C) The stronger the temperature dependence of the rate constant, the smaller is the activation energy.</p><p>(D) If there is no correlation between the temperature and the rate constant then it means that the reaction has negative activation energy.</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "15070f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f923e"}, {"id": "74556e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f923f"}, {"id": "7c30b0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9240"}, {"id": "e762d3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9241"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9242", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52f6"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5660"], "question": {"text": "A reaction has a half life of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>min</mi></math>. The time&nbsp;required for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>99</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>%</mo></math> completion of the reaction is ___ min. (Round off to the Nearest integer)<br />[Use :&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>69</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ln</mi><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn></math>]"}, "options": [{"id": "04b632", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9243"}, {"id": "e6edf9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9244"}, {"id": "b1a05c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9245"}, {"id": "1043d4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9246"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efdc677dc36a88f9247", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4793"], "concepts": ["60e2fb566